 # Data Sources & Attribution
+
+## U.S. groundwater sample and optional static index
+
+The U.S. Groundwater Wells layer includes six historical public USGS monitoring
+locations and supplied sample observations. Credit: U.S. Geological Survey,
+[USGS Water Data](https://waterdata.usgs.gov/). Exact source queries, separate
+retrieval timestamps and byte hashes are preserved in
+[`fixtures/us-groundwater/v1`](fixtures/us-groundwater/v1/README.md).
+USGS-authored public data is in the U.S. public domain; third-party material
+retains separate rights. The software MIT license grants no additional data,
+logo or imagery rights. Preserve original units, datum, dates and qualifiers;
+provisional observations may be revised.
+
+The optional static-index consumer performs no collection. Operator-supplied
+artifacts need their own provenance and rights review. Inventory coverage is
+partial and does not represent all private wells or water availability. See the
+[consumer contract and release order](docs/US_GROUNDWATER_CONSUMER.md).
 
 God's Eye View's **code** is [MIT](LICENSE)-licensed. **The MIT grant covers the source code only — it does NOT extend to third-party data or visual assets.** Every third-party source keeps its own license and terms. This file documents the live and bundled data sources; bundled 3D-model provenance is recorded in [`public/models/README.md`](public/models/README.md).
 
