@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+# U.S. groundwater consumer integration
+
+This is a browser-only consumer for God's Eye View, pinned to upstream commit
+`9d3548c27c2cd4bf80ea39cbb3f0634ab1c5a06b`. It adds the Infrastructure layer
+**U.S. Groundwater Wells**, its source adapter, source attribution, translations,
+share token and tests. It does not include a collector, credentials, national
+dataset, Rust runtime, hosted service or regional research prototypes.
+
+## Producer contract and release order
+
+The independent [Rainfolk producer](https://github.com/Papa-Oso/rainfolk) reference
+is published commit `fc3a6be53d479c150d55c1a6125a2d8ccdd06940`, which includes
+[PR #8](https://github.com/Papa-Oso/rainfolk/pull/8). See its pinned
+[artifact contract](https://github.com/Papa-Oso/rainfolk/blob/fc3a6be53d479c150d55c1a6125a2d8ccdd06940/docs/ARTIFACT_CONTRACT.md)
+and the `well_index` implementation. The contract's
+sentence calling this extension local/uncommitted is historical wording at that
+revision; the pinned source and PR identify the published implementation.
+
+The consumer accepts legacy monolithic count grids and partitioned v2 count
+references while the containing spatial index remains schema version 1. It
+validates immutable references, exact declared byte lengths, SHA-256 digests,
+hierarchy and population conservation before using them. Requests, response
+bytes and caches are bounded. Failed or stale requests cannot replace the
+last-good display; complete coarser aggregates remain the fallback when fine
+detail exceeds budgets. A hash establishes byte integrity, not publisher trust.
+
+**Ship and verify this compatible consumer before activating a v2 index on any
+host.** Producer source publication alone does not activate or publish data.
+Publish immutable referenced files first and the index pointer last; retain the
+previous pointer and its referenced files for rollback. No data hosting change
+is part of this patch.
+
+## Run the bounded sample
+
+Use the upstream supported Node version (24.14.x or 26.x per CONTRIBUTING;
+this package was checked with Node 24.22.1). In a checkout at the pinned GEV base,
+apply the accompanying patch, then:
+
+```sh
+npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
+npm run build
+npm test
+npm run i18n
+npm run check:boundaries
+npm run dev -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4175 --strictPort
+```
+
+Open `http://127.0.0.1:4175/?hv=0#v=2&lat=38&lon=-98&alt=6000000&heading=0&pitch=-90&l=5`.
+The default source is the six-site historical USGS fixture. Keys are not required
+for this layer. Normal upstream basemap/network behavior is unchanged. The sample
+is not a million-record demo and is not evidence of nationwide coverage.
+
+For an operator-supplied static dataset, host a validated producer output at the
+same origin under `/well-index-v1/`, including `index.json` and every referenced
+immutable file, and add `?wellPilot=indexed&hv=0` instead. No such output ships
+with this patch. The adapter permits only a simple same-origin path prefix,
+omits credentials and refuses redirects. It does not call USGS or collect data.
+Embedding applications can inject a `getSnapshot({ signal, bounds, ... })`
+source through the existing application catalog, or use the exported layer and
+single-pack source factories. The standalone indexed selector is optional.
+
+## Interpretation and interaction
+
+The layer-row count is the loaded catalog's total, retained while OFF; the
+represented count describes records represented on the map, including aggregate
+populations. Whole cells intersecting a viewport can include locations outside
+its exact edges: represented counts are not exact within-screen or within-circle
+counts. The shadow circle is visual treatment, not a collection boundary.
+
+Real loaded records render as selectable small dots. Weighted groups use capped
+count markers and split as screen spacing permits. Aggregate centroids never
+masquerade as precise individual wells. Sparse flags and selected detail cards
+reuse GEV's native overlay/context mechanisms beneath its shadow treatment.
+Cards preserve supplied source IDs, dates, signed values, units, vertical
+reference, approval/qualifier flags and official source links. Missing readings
+remain missing. Inventory locations are neither all private wells nor evidence
+of water availability; empty areas mean unknown coverage.
+
+## Verification and upstream handoff
+
+Focused tests live beside the layer and in
+`src/app/usGroundwaterIntegration.test.mjs`; they include legacy/v2 loading,
+count conservation, bounded reads/cache, hashes, stale-load disposal, camera
+updates, native flag selection and OFF/ON ownership. Fixture byte hashes are
+checked by `pack.test.mjs`. Full test/build and browser evidence belongs in the
+accompanying package verification report, not inferred from source inspection.
+Before upstream submission also run the required track/browser gates and verify
+national, dense regional and sparse local views against a deliberately supplied
+dataset. The six-site fixture alone cannot establish national visual quality.
+
+Token `5` is provisional on this pinned base. Upstream
+[PR #1316](https://github.com/bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view/pull/1316) proposes other
+USGS water layers and competing tokens; it explicitly excludes groundwater.
+After rebasing, follow CONTRIBUTING's reservation procedure and rerun
+`npm run layer-token:check -- --base-ref origin/main`. Preserve every published
+assignment. No upstream submission or token reassignment is performed here.
+
+## Rights and provenance
+
+Preserve upstream GEV's MIT license and notices. Original Rainfolk code is MIT;
+the independent producer is referenced, not vendored. USGS data retains its own
+source status and attribution rather than acquiring the software's license.
+The included fixture README, capture URLs/timestamps and hashes identify the six
+public sample records. No logos, imagery, owner/contact corpus or credential
+files are included. See DATA_SOURCES.md and the in-app data attribution entry.
